.TH scene-pack 1 "AUGUST 2026" Linux "User Manuals"
.SH NAME
scene-pack \- package editable SVG scene sources into runtime-safe scene-v1 SVGs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B scene-pack
.BI --input " source.svg"
.BI --output " packed.scene.svg"
[\fB--asset-root\fR \fIPATH\fR]
[\fB--force\fR]
[\fB--check\fR]
[\fB--print-assets\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B scene-pack
embeds linked local PNG images as data URIs, rejects external resources, writes
the packed SVG atomically, and validates the result with the same strict
scene-v1 loader used by i3lock.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --input " PATH"
Editable source SVG.
.TP
.BI --output " PATH"
Packed runtime scene output. Existing files require
.BR --force .
.TP
.BI --asset-root " PATH"
Constrain relative image assets to this root.
.TP
.BI --check
Validate and report what would be embedded without writing output.
.TP
.BI --print-assets
Print each source asset, canonical path, byte size, and MIME type.
.TP
.BI --version
Print the build version.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR i3lock (1),
.BR scene-preview (1)
